From: Project Luma <luma@local>
Subject: [PATCH] Skip unavailable unlock dialog on greetd idle blank

The mobile idle-blank action creates ScreenShield's unlock dialog before it
checks whether locking is enabled. Merely constructing that dialog starts a
GDM reauthentication request, which cannot succeed in the explicit greetd
bake-off session.

Evaluate the existing lock policy before activating ScreenShield. The display
still dims and powers off, the user-active watch is still installed, and wake
still restores the display. Ordinary GNOME sessions retain the full lock path.
---
 js/misc/powerManager.js | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/js/misc/powerManager.js b/js/misc/powerManager.js
--- a/js/misc/powerManager.js
+++ b/js/misc/powerManager.js
@@ -774,13 +774,13 @@ export class PowerManager {
                         () => this._onUserActive().catch(e => console.error(e)));
                 }
 
-                Main.screenShield.activate(false);
-
                 if (cancellable.is_cancelled())
                     return;
 
                 if (!this._lockEnabled())
                     return;
+
+                Main.screenShield.activate(false);
 
                 // try to become modal now already, so that we fail before LOCK_DELAY
                 // in case becoming modal fails
